In the following four cube shapes, A and B are two vertices of the cube, and M, N, P are the midpoints of the edges they are located on. Which of the shapes can be concluded that AB is parallel to the plane MNP?
A. ③④;
B. ①②;
C. ②③;
D. ①④
E.

A geometric solid's three views are shown in the figure. What is the volume of this geometric solid? ( )
A. 12
B. 4
C. \frac{56}{3}
D. \frac{8{\sqrt{3}}}{3}

In the folding process described, if the resulting pentagon DMNPQ is a regular pentagon, and given AB = a, AD = b, DM = m, which of the following conclusions are correct? 
1) $a^{2} - b^{2} = 2ab \tan 18^\circ$; 
2) $m = \sqrt{a^{2} + b^{2}} \cdot \tan 18^\circ$; 
3) $b = m + a \tan 18^\circ$; 
4) $b = \frac{3}{2}m + m \tan 18^\circ$. 
Fill in all correct conclusion numbers.
